e country's top women entrepreneurs  winning several awards such as the  padmashree in 2013 by the government of  india the woman entrepreneur of the year  award in 2010 the rajiv gandhi award in  2008 and many more she was also featured  in fortune magazine's annual listing of  the 50 most powerful women in business  in india for six years in a row from  2011 to 2016. she is properly referred  to as the queen of wellness and became  an inspiration for many homemakers after  her successful venture at number 3 we  have kiran mazumdar shah  she is the founder chairman and managing  director of biocon limited kieran shaw  was born and brought up in bangalore  where she completed her bachelors in  bangalore university  then she went on to do her master's from  melbourne university her story of  starting biocoin india in 1978 out of  the garage in bengaluru has been an  inspiration for many young women she  faced multiple hurdles on the way  starting with a lack of capital to the  challenge of finding qualified workers  however her journey made the difference  in changing lives for the better across  the globe under her backing biocon  delivers on the promise of making  medicines accessible and affordable to  millions of patients worldwide today  biocon india is one of the leading  players in the biomedicine research  space  biocon's profits increased rapidly and  karen shaw became india's wealthiest  self-made woman and her current network  is 3.5 billion dollars according to  forbes she is the recipient of several  awards and accolades including the  prestigious padmashree in 1989 the padma  bhushan in 2005 the utmo gold medal in  2014 and many more at fourth spot we  have indra nui indra novi was born and  brought up in chennai she did a  bachelors in science from madras  christian college in 1974. later she did  a masters in public management from yale  university and a masters in finance and  marketing from iim kolkata she started  as a product manager at johnson and  johnson she later held important  positions at many companies including  motorola and scr brown bubery newey  joined pepsico as senior vice president  of corporate strategy and development in  1994 with the intellect and hard work  she assumed the title of ceo in 2016  and right after that year she became the  chairman of the book  nui was the fifth chairman and ceo of  pepsico's 42 year history and she was  the first ever woman to lead the soft  drink and snack food giant under her  leadership the company's revenue shot  from 35 billion dollars to 63.5 billion  dollars in just one year she was also  awarded the prestigious partner bhushan  for her business achievements this  incredible mind retired from the  position in 2019 and joined amazon.com  as a member of the audit committee at  the board of directors of amazon she has  truly been an inspiration to all of  women kind last but not least we have  aditi gupta in the fifth spot aditi  gupta is an author and co-founder of  menstrupedia this social entrepreneur  was born in jharkhand india to a strict  and orthodox family where people  consider menstruation as a sin  these things confused her until she met  her business come life partner mr tuheen  paul in college disturbed by society's  attitude they wish to educate the masses  they found a severe lack of awareness  about menstruation even among educated  people and this motivated them to  develop the website menstropedia it  provides a user-friendly guide to  menstruation hygiene and puberty while  breaking the myths associated with them  in 2014 menstrual pedia partnered with  whisper india for the school contact  program and presented touch the pickle  which happened in four different cities  in 2014 the comic book she published  reached fame and was translated to  spanish and nepali the famous author  made it to the achievers forbes india 30  in 2014. this mind-blowing author uses  her storytelling skills to educate girls  about menstruation and inspires t